[== a peer's boot with the modern graph: boot/peer.mtron plus the grph instset and g:, a TinkerGraph loaded with the
     MODERN dataset under the modern schema, the graph the live server (drstynx.boot.mtron) mounts at g:. Every peer
     loads the same ids, so a vertex address such as g:V/4 names the same vertex on every machine, and a lane that walks
     the graph (out(), in(), both()) finds its types (person::T, software::T), its instructions and its data where it
     lands.
       {3,4}.harvest(<boot/space/grph/peer.boot.mtron>) ==]
import(/m/sys);
import(/m/math,math);
import(/m/math/cat,cat);
import(/m/web,web);
import(/m/db/grph);
[== peers discover peers ==]
mdns_discovery::[=>];
fsspace::[pattern=>fs:#,
          route  => [fs: => <~>]]@~/memory/space/fs;
[== the modern graph at g: ==]
grphspace::[pattern => g:#,
            q       => [incrq::[=>],subq::[=>]],
            schema  => !*/m/db/grph/schema/modern,
            config  => [
              dataset         => <org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.LoadGraphWith.GraphData.MODERN>,
              <gremlin.graph> => <org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.tinkergraph.structure.TinkerGraph>],
            route   => [g: => <>]]@<~/memory/space/grph/g>;
[== peers create peers: every peer can harvest peers of its own, which makes it an interior node of a tree. From the
     root, branch(<//0> => {2,3}.harvest(<boot/space/grph/peer.boot.mtron>), <//1> => {4,5}.harvest(<…>)) has //0
     dial //2 and //3 and //1 dial //4 and //5, and a plan with a budget of two (sum?hop=2(), repeat?<=A{*}&hop=2(…))
     re-deals at //0 and //1. A number is a port on this host (n + 1111), so each peer in the tree takes its own. ==]
harvest?rec<=int{*}(uri{?}::T){
  spawn?uri<=int(<//localhost:${_ + 1111}/${_}>,<//${_}>,*0).
    -<[host=>_].as(ws_client::T).barrier()>>host.>-[,].as(rec::T)}@harvest;
